[
  {
    "id": "tab-octopus-main",
    "type": "tab",
    "label": "Octopus Intelligent Dashboard",
    "disabled": false,
    "info": "# Octopus Intelligent Dashboard 2.0 Example\n\nThis is a **teaching example** showing how to wire the `octopus-intelligent` node to a [@flowfuse/node-red-dashboard](https://github.com/FlowFuse/node-red-dashboard) (Dashboard 2.0) UI.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Install `@flowfuse/node-red-dashboard` via the Node-RED Palette Manager.\n2. Open the **Octopus Intelligent** node and enter your real Account Number and API Key.\n3. Deploy, then open the dashboard at `http://<node-red-host>:1880/dashboard`.\n\n## Pages\n\n- **Controls** — writable controls that send commands back to the node's input port\n- **Status** — EV charging status, slots, and window\n- **Tariff** — current rates, rate stats, rate bands\n- **Optimization** — sample derivation logic on the `applicable_rates` array (see below)\n- **Account** — balance, Octoplus, Saving Sessions, Free Electricity, Home Mini\n- **Diagnostics** — API usage, version, per-category error list\n\n## Sample Function Nodes (USER-MODIFIABLE)\n\nThe **Optimization** page contains two function nodes marked `SAMPLE`. These are **not** part of the node's published payload — they demonstrate patterns for deriving custom values from `applicable_rates`. Edit them freely for your use case:\n\n- `find-cheapest-window`: Slides a configurable-duration window over the rate schedule to find the cheapest contiguous block starting in the future.\n- `is-cheapest-now`: Returns `true` when the current rate equals the day's minimum — useful as an automation trigger.\n\n## Writable Controls\n\nControls on the Controls page route back to the Octopus Intelligent node's **input** port via change nodes:\n\n| Control | Payload sent |\n|---|---|\n| Target Limit (number input) | `{ set_limit: <value> }` |\n| Ready By (dropdown) | `{ set_time: \"HH:MM\" }` |\n| Smart Charging (switch) | `{ set_smart_charging: true\\|false }` |\n| Refresh (button) | `{ refresh: true }` (any non-command object triggers refresh) |\n| Timezone (text input) | `{ set_timezone: \"Region/City\" }` |"
  },
